  "worked_solution": "Let's go through each of the options.\n\n- The function $f(y)$  is not homogeneous. It is a polynomial of degree $2.$ However, it also contains a term ($y$) that is of degree $1.$ Therefore, not all of its terms are of degree $2.$\n\n- The function $g(x,y)$ is homogeneous of degree $4.$ It is a polynomial of degree $4,$ and all of its terms are of degree $4.$\n\n- The function $h(x,y,z)$ is homogeneous of degree $3.$ It is a polynomial of degree $3,$ with no terms of degree other than $3.$",
